        <name>withoutNullValues</name>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Mode to enable or disable skipping null child pointers.</para><para>The <ref refid="classRoseAst_1_1iterator_1aa38271b735f7bc9216d5b03d7ad686bf" kindref="member">withoutNullValues</ref> mode causes the iterator to skip over null child pointers, while the <ref refid="classRoseAst_1_1iterator_1aa844845daf11f00a0549e04dd0b96166" kindref="member">withNullValues</ref> mode causse null child pointers to be followed followed. The mode affects subsequent advancement of the iterator, not its current value. In other words, in the <ref refid="classRoseAst_1_1iterator_1aa844845daf11f00a0549e04dd0b96166" kindref="member">withNullValues</ref> mode the iterator dereference operator will always return non-null values after its next increment. The default mode is <ref refid="classRoseAst_1_1iterator_1aa38271b735f7bc9216d5b03d7ad686bf" kindref="member">withoutNullValues</ref>.</para><para>The function returns this iterator and can therefore be called together with <ref refid="classRoseAst_1a6058ab784c5b0ca4e1f977c0f78f045f" kindref="member">begin</ref>, like this:</para><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">RoseAst::iterator<sp/>i<sp/>=<sp/>ast.begin().withNullValues();</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>        </detaileddescription>
